The four sets, their sources and what was changed:

`tests/handwritten/gold_de_en/`

  "Gold", German Wikipedia, by Wikipedia contributors
  https://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gold
  The article's revision history, reached from that page, lists its authors.
  Used in: source_a.md

  "Gold", English Wikipedia, by Wikipedia contributors
  https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gold
  The article's revision history, reached from that page, lists its authors.
  Used in: source_b.md

  Changes: Each source is an excerpt of one article. The text was shortened and its formatting simplified.

`tests/handwritten/mahjongg/`

  "Mah-Jongg", German Wikipedia, by Wikipedia contributors
  https://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mah-Jongg
  The article's revision history, reached from that page, lists its authors.
  Used in: source_a.md, source_b.md, source_c.md and reference.md

  Changes: The three sources are excerpts of the article, shortened, with simplified formatting, and divided across three files out of their original order. `reference.md` is the project author's merge of the three.

`tests/handwritten/sepia/`

  "Cuttlefish", English Wikipedia, by Wikipedia contributors
  https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cuttlefish
  The article's revision history, reached from that page, lists its authors.
  Used in: source_a.md, source_b.md and reference.md

  Changes: The two sources are excerpts of the article, shortened and with simplified formatting. `reference.md` is the two sources joined.

`tests/handwritten/treecreeper/`

  "Eurasian treecreeper", English Wikipedia, by Wikipedia contributors
  https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eurasian_treecreeper
  The article's revision history, reached from that page, lists its authors.
  Used in: source_a.md, source_b.md, source_c.md and reference.md

  Changes: The three sources are three sections of the article, shortened and with simplified formatting. `reference.md` is the three sources joined.

